  "result": "Perfect! All 192 tests pass. I've successfully added voucher support to the invoicing system:\n\n**src/invoices.js** - Added new function:\n\n**applyVoucher(invoice, { code, amount })** - Applies a fixed-amount discount:\n- Validates invoice status is 'draft' (NOT_DRAFT error for non-draft invoices)\n- Enforces one voucher per invoice (VOUCHER_EXISTS error if already applied)\n- Validates amount is a positive integer (AMOUNT_INVALID for zero, negative, or fractional)\n- Stores voucher with code and amount\n- Returns ok(newInvoice) with invoice.voucher set\n- Never mutates input invoice\n\n**Updated invoiceTotals**:\n- Now returns `{ subtotal, discount, vat, voucher, total }`\n- `voucher`: the amount of the voucher (0 if not applied)\n- `total`: subtotal - discount + vat - voucher (clamped at 0)\n- Allows generous vouchers that exceed the total (clamped to 0)\n\n**src/errors.js** - Added error code:\n- `VOUCHER_EXISTS`: \"This invoice already has a voucher applied.\"\n\n**Tests** - 11 new tests covering:\n- Applying vouchers to draft invoices\n- Rejecting non-draft invoices\n- Preventing multiple vouchers on same invoice\n- Amount validation (zero, negative, non-integer)\n- Input immutability\n- invoiceTotals with and without vouchers\n- Correct total calculation with vouchers\n- Clamping when voucher exceeds total\n- Zero voucher amount when not applied\n\nThe implementation allows any positive integer amount and calculates the final total as `subtotal - discount + vat - voucher`, with the total automatically clamped at zero to prevent negative invoice totals.",
